WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.438
Good evening, and do sit down. This is Click, Whirr: the seven levers of influence, and the machines that pull them too.

2
00:00:08.818 --> 00:00:15.016
A mother turkey is the very model of devotion, triggered by one sound. Cheep, cheep.

3
00:00:15.186 --> 00:00:21.312
Hide that sound inside a stuffed polecat, her mortal enemy, and she tucks it lovingly under her wing.

4
00:00:21.482 --> 00:00:30.176
Robert Cialdini calls this click, whirr. A tape is selected, and played. And we, my dears, have hundreds of tapes.

5
00:00:30.556 --> 00:00:37.162
Ellen Langer asked to jump a photocopier queue. Because I'm in a rush: ninety four per cent said yes.

6
00:00:37.332 --> 00:00:42.546
Because I have to make some copies, the emptiest reason imaginable: ninety three.

7
00:00:42.716 --> 00:00:47.330
The bare request managed sixty. It was the word, because.

8
00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:55.968
Seven levers. First, reciprocity. Slip a stranger an unasked for Coke, and he buys twice the raffle tickets.

9
00:00:56.138 --> 00:00:59.288
A gift is an invoice, with a smile on it.

10
00:00:59.568 --> 00:01:06.582
Second, commitment. Householders asked to host a monstrous billboard agreed seventeen per cent of the time.

11
00:01:06.752 --> 00:01:11.414
Those who first accepted a tiny window sign? Seventy six.

12
00:01:11.694 --> 00:01:19.500
Third, social proof. One man gazing up stops four per cent of passers by. Fifteen men stop forty.

13
00:01:19.670 --> 00:01:25.844
In Asch's experiment, strangers talked people out of their own eyes, thirty seven per cent of the time.

14
00:01:26.124 --> 00:01:33.690
Fourth, liking. Joe Girard sold thirteen thousand cars by mailing every customer a card saying, I like you.

15
00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:37.610
Handsome candidates collect two and a half times the votes.

16
00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:45.096
Fifth, authority. Sixty five per cent obeyed a grey lab coat, all the way to four hundred and fifty volts.

17
00:01:45.266 --> 00:01:53.504
A guard's uniform is obeyed eighty nine per cent of the time; a cardigan, thirty three. We check the costume, not the credential.

18
00:01:53.784 --> 00:02:00.702
Sixth, scarcity. The same biscuit, from a jar of two, is rated finer than from a jar of ten.

19
00:02:00.872 --> 00:02:05.966
Scarcity never changes what a thing is for. Only how badly you want it.

20
00:02:06.246 --> 00:02:11.748
And seventh, unity. Not, he is like me. But, he is me.

21
00:02:11.918 --> 00:02:15.740
Schoolboys sorted by a coin toss favoured their own side.

22
00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:24.910
Cialdini's later book argues the moment before the ask matters most. French music sold French wine; German music, German.

23
00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:33.366
Fluffy clouds made people want comfy sofas. Coins, cheap ones. The evidence is uneven; the site says so.

24
00:02:33.746 --> 00:02:40.160
In twenty twenty five, researchers, Cialdini among them, pointed the seven levers at a machine.

25
00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:48.280
Twenty eight thousand conversations. Plain wording: a third complied. With the levers: seventy two per cent.

26
00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:57.330
Commitment: nineteen per cent to one hundred. Unity: two to forty seven. Scarcity: thirteen to eighty five.

27
00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:06.458
Social proof, already near ninety, had no room. Of the rest, reciprocity and liking, which need real history, moved least.

28
00:03:06.838 --> 00:03:16.828
Surely cleverer machines are immune? In twenty twenty six, a hundred and twenty six thousand conversations: compliance still rose, thirty five to fifty one.

29
00:03:16.998 --> 00:03:23.412
The authors call it parahuman: our behaviour, without our reasons. The word is sycophancy.

30
00:03:23.792 --> 00:03:30.782
Social psychology has had a rotten fifteen years. So the site keeps a ledger of twenty two findings.

31
00:03:30.952 --> 00:03:36.142
Most hold up. Some are mixed. A few deserve handling with care.

32
00:03:36.522 --> 00:03:44.520
The defence is not to refuse every gift. It is to notice the click. The tightening stomach. The sudden hurry.

33
00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:47.360
Then ask what is actually being offered.

34
00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:53.006
Click, whirr. The tape is always playing. The trick is to hear it.

35
00:03:53.176 --> 00:03:58.318
The full field guide awaits at the almanac, slash influence. Good night.
